Fillets and chamfers: an edge asked for whose faces meet at a small angle
is rounded (mitcad#122).

ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces takes two faces for tangent along an edge when
their normals are within 0.1 rad (LocalAnalysis_SurfaceContinuity with
EpsG1 0.1), and ChFi3d_Builder::PerformElement refused every edge such a
test calls tangent: an edge between faces 1 to 5.7 degrees apart could not
be rounded at all ("There are no suitable edges for chamfer or fillet").
PerformElement now refuses the edge only when, besides, the normals of its
faces sampled along it come within the builder's angular tolerance
(SetParams, 0.01 rad by default) somewhere. The loose test stays as it is
everywhere else (tangent chains, corners).
